  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 1,
      "comment": "Inoculated filters were transferred to 47-mm-diameter petri dishes (Millipore) containing Whatman glass fiber filters presaturated with 1.5 ml of medium DH (Castenholz’s medium D) (PMID: 4984428) supplemented with HEPES buffer at 1.2 g/liter and pH 8.2 (the approximate pH of the mat at this site)."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "comment": "Designed by R. P. Sheridan, medium D is prepared as a 10-fold concentrated stock and stored at 4 C unautoclaved."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 8,
      "comment": "The pH is adjusted after dilution (double-distilled water) to 8.2 with 1 M NaOH."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 9,
      "comment": "The final pH is 7.5 to 7.6 after the autoclaved medium has cooled and cleared completely."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 10,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 12,
      "comment": ""
    }
  ]
}